Description: GPU-accelerated compression tool with Qt GUI
 nvCOMP is a high-performance compression toolkit that leverages
 NVIDIA CUDA for GPU-accelerated compression and decompression.
 It supports multiple algorithms including LZ4, Zstd, Snappy,
 GDeflate, ANS, and Bitcomp.
 .
 Features:
  - Modern Qt6 graphical interface
  - Automatic GPU/CPU fallback
  - Multi-volume support for large files
  - Folder/directory compression
  - Cross-platform compatibility
  - Desktop integration (file associations, context menus)
 .
 This package includes the GUI application, CLI tool, and
 file manager integration for Nautilus and Nemo.

Package: nvcomp-cli
Architecture: amd64
Breaks: nvcomp-gui (<< 1.0.0-2)
Replaces: nvcomp-gui (<< 1.0.0-2)
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends},
         libstdc++6 (>= 10),
         libc6 (>= 2.31)
Recommends: nvidia-driver (>= 580) | nvidia-driver-580
Suggests: nvidia-smi
Description: GPU-accelerated compression tool (CLI only)
 nvCOMP is a high-performance compression toolkit that leverages
 NVIDIA CUDA for GPU-accelerated compression and decompression.
 .
 This package provides only the command-line interface (CLI)
 for nvcomp without GUI dependencies. It's ideal for servers
 and automation.
 .
 Supported algorithms:
  - LZ4 (fast, good ratio)
  - Zstd (best ratio)
  - Snappy (fastest)
  - GDeflate, ANS, Bitcomp (GPU-only)

Package: nvcomp-dev
Architecture: amd64
Depends: nvcomp-gui (= ${binary:Version}) | nvcomp-cli (= ${binary:Version}),
         ${misc:Depends}
Description: Development files for nvCOMP
 Development headers and libraries for nvCOMP compression
 toolkit. Allows developers to integrate nvCOMP functionality
 into their own applications.
 .
 This package contains:
  - C and C++ header files
  - Static and shared libraries
  - Example code
  - API documentation

